SCORE: SUCCFAN-CURV-RQ | behavior_evidence=3 | geometry_necessity=2 | novelty=3 | downstream_mechanism=4 | falsifiability=4 | implementability=3 | exploration_value=3
SCOPE: SUCCFAN-CURV-RQ | IN_SCOPE | Behaviour (popularity-adjusted directed fanout f_i from training transitions, E2) and geometry (per-prefix c_p through lambda_p=2/(1-c_p||x||^2) in the encode/decode residual chain, E12/E13) lie on one pathway, and behaviour-off (c_p=1), geometry-off (c->0, lambda=1) and both-on exist. Missing from the visible specification: the functional form c_p=F(f_p) and a derived bound keeping c_p||x||^2<1; the (0.1,10) clip is an un-derived constant (a policy gap, not a scope violation).
EVIDENCE: SUCCFAN-CURV-RQ | E2 E5 E6 E7 E8 E10 E11 E12 E13
OBJECTION: The conformal factor acts only as a positive scalar multiplier on the residual before a Euclidean argmin, so the mechanism is a per-prefix temperature; additionally no guard keeps c_p||x||^2<1 while the clip (0.1,10) is hard-coded, so the claimed <1% overhead is unbounded near the ball boundary.
COUNTEREXAMPLE: For every lambda>0 and every Euclidean residual r, argmin_j ||lambda*r - c_j||_2 = argmin_j ||r - c_j/lambda||_2, so a Euclidean RQ level with the per-prefix codebook {c_j/lambda_p} reproduces the level-l assignment exactly and the conformal factor changes no ranking a codebook rescale cannot. As c_p||x||^2 -> 1, lambda -> infinity and the amplified residual, not curvature, dominates the loss.
RATIONALE: SUCCFAN-CURV-RQ: behaviour 3 - E5 measures strongly stratified successor entropy (top-1 mass 0.4375 vs 0.0543, Spearman -0.973) and E10 measures the transition graph (115582 distinct edges, mean out-degree 5.45), so the signal is real, but the premise that flat code resolution is the binding constraint is unmeasured and E8 pulls the other way (K=16 cluster share 0.3106 vs 0.0822 at K=256), so not 4. geometry 2 - the identity above: the curved object is a scalar and the metric is unchanged. novelty 3 - a per-prefix curvature field is a distinct computation relative to the measured l1_br / successor_geodesic_coarse / tangent_successor_residual runs, but computationally it is a per-prefix temperature schedule. downstream 4 - level-l assignment, observables (code entropy in the top-fanout quartile, prefix-conditional next-code accuracy) and expected direction are named; the step "the generator exploits finer hub codes" is asserted. falsifiability 4 - three switches, a 0.065 criterion and a mechanism-idle diagnostic, but the matched Euclidean arm is only the c->0 limit and is not argued as a distinct control. implementability 3 - differentiable scalar ops and <1% FLOPs, but no guard on 1-c||x||^2 and an un-derived clip. exploration 3 - a different corner of the same successor-quantizer family; a negative says resolution adaptation is not the lever. Coverage of E11's same-first-prefix statistic is UNKNOWN; a bounded validation-split check (n and CI for 0.0907 vs 0.067) would resolve whether the SID hypothesis follows.

SCORE: cocond-markov-poincare-ot | behavior_evidence=3 | geometry_necessity=3 | novelty=4 | downstream_mechanism=4 | falsifiability=4 | implementability=3 | exploration_value=4
SCOPE: cocond-markov-poincare-ot | IN_SCOPE | Behaviour is the training-only popularity-adjusted transition matrix diffused into the OT plan (E1-E3); geometry is the Poincare ground cost, Mobius maps and the Einstein barycenter inside the same assignment block (E12/E13); removing behaviour changes P and the barycenter weights while removing curvature changes K and the mean operator, so the coupling is real. Missing from the visible text: the derivation of alpha (it says "see SAFEGUARDS", absent from the bundle), the definition of the column prior q, and explicit USE_BEHAVIOUR/USE_HYPERBOLIC flags with the three named comparisons - the hypothesis names only the unmodified Euclidean baseline.
EVIDENCE: cocond-markov-poincare-ot | E5 E6 E7 E8 E10 E11 E12 E13
OBJECTION: The Markov step is applied to a B x B batch submatrix of a sparse item graph, so most rows are empty and the diffusion is an identity (P <- (1-alpha)P) for the majority of items; the stated 5-8 MFLOP cost holds only for a sparse kernel, while a dense (1024x1024)@(1024x256) kernel is about three orders larger.
COUNTEREXAMPLE: With B=1024, N=24556 and mean out-degree 5.45 (E10), the expected number of in-batch successors is 5.45*(1024/24556)=0.227; under Poisson, P(no in-batch successor)=e^-0.227~0.80. For those >=80% of rows B_bt@P=0, so behaviour-on equals behaviour-off; the remaining rows shrink mass toward a neighbour average rather than transport a behaviour signal. Dense cost is 3 iterations * 3 levels * 1024^2*256 ~ 7.2 GFLOP per step, not 5-8 MFLOP.
RATIONALE: cocond-markov-poincare-ot: behaviour 3 - E10 and E5 establish a real but sparse transition signal and E11 shows baseline SIDs carry only a small successor structure (0.0907 vs null 0.067), which supports the motivation and also caps what is exploitable. geometry 3 - Poincare cost, Mobius addition and Einstein barycenter are genuine curved computations, but a matched Euclidean OT with Euclidean barycenter is never argued to be insufficient. novelty 4 - moving the assignment plan with an OT diffusion is a distinct computation relative to the measured l1_br / successor_geodesic_coarse / tangent_successor_residual runs, and the argument against them is explicit. downstream 4 - plan change, prefix hit-rate/conditional-entropy observables and directions are named; the last step to recall depends on the generator. falsifiability 4 - the three removals are described and the "if (a) rises but (c) does not" failure diagnosis is explicit, but the switches are prose, not named code flags. implementability 3 - Sinkhorn is differentiable and eps-guarded, but alpha and q are unspecified in the visible spec, the Einstein midpoint is called a "3-vector Klein map" although the latent is d-dimensional (a dimensional ambiguity), and the cost claim needs sparse kernels. exploration 4 - a genuinely different failure mode (assignment-level coupling) whose negative would be informative. Alpha derivation, q and the 3-vector/d-dimensional issue are UNKNOWN in the frozen bundle; reading the referenced SAFEGUARDS section and confirming the Klein-map dimension would resolve them.

SCORE: CURVCELL-SID | behavior_evidence=3 | geometry_necessity=3 | novelty=3 | downstream_mechanism=4 | falsifiability=4 | implementability=4 | exploration_value=4
SCOPE: CURVCELL-SID | IN_SCOPE | Behaviour is the effective successor branching B[l][k]=exp(H) of each current code cell from training transitions (E1-E3); geometry is per-code kappa[l][k] entering the argmin d_B(eps,c)/sqrt(kappa), the commitment term and the Mobius residual (E12/E13); the behaviour-off (single unit curvature) and geometry-off (keep behaviour weights, remove curvature) switches are stated. Missing from the visible text: the exact clamp for s[l][k] and how the base measure of d_B is kept consistent when kappa varies.
EVIDENCE: CURVCELL-SID | E5 E6 E7 E8 E10 E11 E12 E13
OBJECTION: B[l][k] is measured on the same partition it then resizes, and the entropy of a successor-code histogram is mechanically non-decreasing in cell size (more items contribute more distinct successor codes), so the proposed "Spearman(|A_k|, B_k) clearly positive" diagnostic can be satisfied with no behavioural coupling and the cumulative-mean refresh has a rich-get-richer collapse mode.
COUNTEREXAMPLE: Let a cell hold n items whose successors are i.i.d. draws from one fixed distribution over K codes. The expected number of distinct successor codes is K*(1-(1-1/K)^n), which rises with n; hence B_k rises with |A_k| even when every item has identical behaviour, s_k then grows and the cell grows further. The Spearman diagnostic is confounded by cell size alone.
RATIONALE: CURVCELL-SID: behaviour 3 - E5's entropy quintiles (top-1 mass 0.4375 to 0.0543, support 2.8 to 44.3) and E10's 115582 edges support a real branching statistic, but that geodesic budget is the binding constraint is a hypothesis and E8 shows level-1 granularity has a large first-order effect, so the lever is not isolated. geometry 3 - Mobius/Poincare distance is genuinely curved and the per-code scale interacts with its position-dependent metric, but the behaviour-conditioned part is one positive scalar per code (a temperature) and a matched Euclidean per-code temperature is not ruled out. novelty 3 - co-evolving the curvature field with the partition is a distinct computation relative to the measured l1_br / geodesic-coarse / tangent runs, but a co-proposal lists "per-branch curvature" as an earlier-round mechanism, in which case the only new part is the refresh loop (a routine variation, 2); the ledger entry is UNKNOWN from the frozen bundle and a bounded check of the round ledger would resolve it. downstream 4 - the argmin with /s, the observables and the expected direction are named, though the Spearman observable is confounded as above. falsifiability 4 - three switches, a 0.065 criterion and the "|A_k| vs B_k near zero means encoder absorbed the behaviour" falsifier are present, but one diagnostic is confounded and the controls are prose rather than named flags. implementability 4 - equations, a budget-derived refresh schedule, no gradient into s, tanh/eps guards, +2-4% cost and named risks; the missing explicit clamp and the non-metric distance keep it from 5. exploration 4 - a self-consistent cell-size field is substantially different and a negative would show that adaptive resolution does not convert into recall.